            <ArticleTitle>Temporomandibular joint dysfunction and orofacial pain caused by parotid gland malignancy: report of case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>348-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 41-year-old female with 2 years of mandibular and maxillary facial pain sought multiple medical evaluations. Symptoms were similar to those accompanying many benign temporomandibular, salivary gland, and neurological disorders. Through manual palpation, a slight swelling in the salivary gland was discovered; a malignant carcinoma was removed by parotidectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
